Build Your Own Climate Scenario -- licensing
======================================================================

This repository holds three kinds of material, and each carries its own terms.
The full text of the terms lives at https://thehonestbroker.org/terms/

1. CODE -- the build scripts, analysis pipeline and site source.
   MIT licence, reproduced in full below.

2. WRITING AND FIGURES -- the page copy, the explanatory text and the chart
   designs published at https://scenarios.thehonestbroker.org
   Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivatives 4.0 International (CC BY-ND 4.0)
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nd/4.0/
   Copy and redistribute them, commercially included, with credit and a link
   back. Do not distribute an altered version.

3. DERIVED DATA -- the JSON, CSV and spreadsheet series this repository
   produces and publishes.
   Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   Use, adapt and build on them, commercially included, with a citation.

NOT COVERED. The upstream observations are not mine to license. Most originate
with US federal agencies and carry no copyright under 17 U.S.C. sec. 105;
ERA5 and other Copernicus products arrive under the Copernicus licence, which
travels with the data. See the project's methodology or sources page for the
per-dataset terms.

TEXT AND DATA MINING. Rights are reserved under Art. 4(3) of EU Directive
2019/790 and the equivalent provisions elsewhere. Training a machine-learning
model on this material needs written permission: roger.pielke@aei.org

TRADEMARK. "The Honest Broker" and the associated logo sit outside every
licence above. No Creative Commons or MIT licence grants trademark rights.

